  "bio": {
    "eyebrow": "About Dr Geng",
    "heading_lead": "Meet",
    "heading_warm": "Dr Geng.",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Dr Tao Geng is an independent Consultant Specialist GP (ABN: 43 100 136 624) (MED0001670974) consulting at the Earlwood / Bangor centres.",
      "Before coming to Australia, Dr Tao Geng graduated from Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine and worked as a general physician in Shanghai for five years. She passed her Australian Medical Council (AMC) exams and undertook her internship and resident training in St Vincent's Hospital Sydney and Wagga Wagga Base Hospital. She also had her paediatric training in Canterbury Hospital. Dr Geng completed her GP training in rural NSW towns, including Wagga Wagga and Leeton.",
      "Dr Geng has now moved back to Sydney. She enjoys looking after patients' general health and disease prevention. She is especially interested in paediatrics, women's health, antenatal shared care, and skin lesions.",
      "Dr Geng is the Honorary Treasurer of the Australasian Medical Services Coalition (AMSC) in the community. With her strong track record of voluntary work in the community, in 2019, Dr Geng was recognized and presented by Mr Mark Coure MP for the St George Community Award in the category of Individual Volunteer Achievement Award. With her exemplary and outstanding service to the organisation, she was awarded the Outstanding Achievement Award of the Australian Chinese Medical Association in 2019.",
      "Dr Geng speaks English and Mandarin, as well as Shanghainese."
    ]
  },
  "fellowships": [
    "Consultant Specialist GP",
